{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You shall not have.</b> Scripture speaks of Elohim in accordance with the thought of His worshippers, like 'and Hananiah the prophet took' (Jeremiah 28:10), and 'the men pursued after them' (Joshua 2:7), and so Samuel said, 'Why have you disturbed me?' (I Samuel 28:15), for Scripture spoke according to Saul's thought — and this is not the place to explain it." "And the meaning of 'upon My face' is like 'and Haran died upon the face of Terah his father' (Genesis 11:28), that he was present with him and saw his death, and likewise, 'and Eleazar and Ithamar ministered upon the face of Aaron their father' (Numbers 3:4). And behold, the meaning is: after 'I am your Elohim,' and I am present always in every place, and I see what you do — it is not fitting that you associate other gods with Me. And one of the wise of heart said: 'Do not anger your master while he is looking at you.' And behold, this commandment, which is 'you shall not have,' is in the heart and also in the mouth, for there is no negative commandment in the Torah that is in the heart except this one. For a person who says before witnesses that he is going to murder or to commit adultery is not put to death on account of his speech if he did no deed; but one who says, 'Let us go and serve other gods' — Scripture commanded, 'you shall surely kill him' (Deuteronomy 13:10). And in deed: <b>You shall not make for yourself a carved image or any likeness</b> of wood or stone, and you shall not make by any craft a likeness that is in the heavens. And it says 'from above' — for they are above the earth from every side, and there are no likenesses in the heavens, only forty-eight forms, and the masters of the forms make things that are not so, and their deeds are close to idol worship."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {1 "The numbering of Deuteronomy references may vary between witnesses; the citation 'you shall surely kill him' corresponds to the law of the inciter (Deut 13:10 in Hebrew versification, 13:9 in some English)."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:11.485561537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}